<p>Commonly used APIs are available without an <code>import</code> statement, powered by <a href="https://github.com/unjs/unimport">unimport</a> and <a href="https://github.com/unplugin/unplugin-vue-components">unplugin-vue-components</a>. Only what you use ends up in the bundle.</p>

{% include preview with { demo: 'auto-imports', title: 'No imports in this component' } %}

{% include code_block with { lang: 'vue', title: 'templates/demos/vue/mouse-tracker.visible.ce.vue', code: source('@uebertool_docs/demos/vue/mouse-tracker.visible.ce.vue') } only %}

<h2>What is available</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Vue</td><td><code>ref</code>, <code>computed</code>, <code>watch</code>, <code>onMounted</code>, …</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pinia</td><td><code>defineStore</code>, <code>storeToRefs</code>, …</td></tr>
    <tr><td>VueUse</td><td><code>useMouse</code>, <code>useIntervalFn</code>, … (except <code>toRef</code> and <code>toValue</code>, which come from Vue)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Alpine.js</td><td><code>Alpine</code> (default export of <code>alpinejs</code>)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Your code</td><td>Every export of a file in <code>js/**</code>, e.g. <code>formatMs</code> from <code>js/utils/formatMs.ts</code></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

{% embed aside with { type: 'caution', title: 'templates/ is not scanned' } %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>The default configuration also lists <code>./templates/**/*.{js|ts}</code>, but the glob uses <code>|</code> instead of <code>,</code> and matches nothing. Put shared code into <code>js/</code>, e.g. <code>js/utils</code>, which is not an entrypoint.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}

<h2>Components</h2>
<p>Components are resolved by name in Vue templates:</p>
<ul>
  <li>your <code>*.ce.vue</code> files in <code>js/</code> and <code>templates/</code> that have no loading strategy,</li>
  <li><a href="https://headlessui.com">Headless UI</a> components,</li>
  <li>VueUse components and directives.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Types</h2>
<p>Declarations are generated into <code>.uebertool/unimport.d.ts</code> and <code>.uebertool/components.d.ts</code>, both included by the <a href="{{ path('uebertool_docs_pages.page', { slug: 'types' }) }}">generated tsconfig</a>.</p>

<h2>Configuration</h2>
<p>The <code>unimport</code> and <code>components</code> options are deep-merged with the defaults, so arrays such as <code>presets</code> and <code>dirs</code> are extended, not replaced:</p>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'ts', title: 'vite.config.ts' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
uebertool({
  unimport: {
    dirs: ['./js/composables/**/*'],
    imports: [{ name: 'gsap', from: 'gsap' }],
  },
})
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

{% embed aside with { type: 'caution' } %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>Presets are resolved from your theme directory. Install <code>@vueuse/core</code> (and <code>pinia</code>, if you use it) in the theme itself.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
